        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 90-year-old male patient, admitted on 10/02/2000 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination revealed prolonged expiration and diffuse wheezing. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis demonstrated hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory markers. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and intravenous fluids. Oxygen saturation was closely monitored throughout. The patient showed satisfactory clinical improvement and was discharged on 11/02/2000. I recommend continuation of his inhaled maintenance therapy and close outpatient follow-up. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
